@startuml
title Patch Release Publish Lane
left to right direction
skinparam Shadowing false
skinparam DefaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam ArrowColor #1d4f73
skinparam Rectangle {
  BorderColor #1d4f73
  BackgroundColor #eef6fb
  FontColor #0f172a
  RoundCorner 12
}
skinparam Note {
  BorderColor #8b6f2f
  BackgroundColor #fff7d6
  FontColor #3f3420
}

rectangle "Retained maintenance branch\nfor example release/3.1" as branch
rectangle "Patch change on maintenance branch\nor MR targeting maintenance release/*" as patch
rectangle "Release validation lane\nre-runs on the reviewed patch tip" as validate
rectangle "Intentional web/api publish start\nSOK_PIPELINE_MODE=release_publish\non protected maintenance branch" as trigger
rectangle "Fetch retained release candidate\nfrom current maintenance branch\nfetch-release-candidate" as fetch
rectangle "Promote validated patch outputs\npublish-release-images\npublish-release-artifacts\npublish-release-bundle\npublish-release-charts" as publish #eefbf1
rectangle "Certification and submission prep\npreflight-certification\nprepare-certified-operators-submission\nprepare-community-operators-submission" as downstream #f7f7ff
rectangle "GitLab Release record\nfor patch version" as release_record #f7f7ff
rectangle "Forward-port patch to main\nseparate change-management step" as forward_port

branch --> patch
patch --> validate
validate --> trigger
trigger --> fetch
fetch --> publish
publish --> downstream
downstream --> release_record
release_record --> forward_port

note bottom of trigger
Patch publication does not require merging the
maintenance branch into main first.
end note

note bottom of forward_port
Forward-port the released patch back to main after the
patch release is cut so the trunks do not diverge.
end note
@enduml
